{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players, Ava, Beau, and Cato, are playing a tournament. Each person plays exactly two games, one game against each of the other players. If a game ends in a tie, both players are awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Otherwise, the winning player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points and the losing player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p>For example, if the tournament results are as shown below and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a394e53ae5d9485467a5da722ed2d61c63077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then points are awarded as follows:\n</p><p>(add a table to the Problem 2 page)\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the points that have been awarded to the three players when the tournament has finished. In the example above, Ava is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point, Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> in the example.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f5a27672aa67b8089928196ac71ab0210f71f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, how many games ended in a tie?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd46d9508b388af41f4e3d7f16ce41e6c18b8bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> be the number of games that were tied and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6053907b455e0ef20a366e07f007ac4fc0eb002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of games that resulted in one person winning and the other losing. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people are involved in each game and each gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point from every game that ties, the total number of points increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34a068fc593714a83c298e0e3570977270c1c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> for each game that is tied. Also, according to the rules and the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f5a27672aa67b8089928196ac71ab0210f71f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, each game where someone wins, the total number of points increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for each game where someone wins and another person loses.\n</p><p>This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43ce754c5feaf3a1b26480bea8209d4d8aed61eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2g_1 + 4g_2 = S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to make it easier to see what the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd46d9508b388af41f4e3d7f16ce41e6c18b8bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6053907b455e0ef20a366e07f007ac4fc0eb002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> are, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c0df9dd57b9ebfea08a539d619050a88b0ad420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 + 2g_2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd46d9508b388af41f4e3d7f16ce41e6c18b8bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6053907b455e0ef20a366e07f007ac4fc0eb002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> are non-negative integers, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/76953c3888af8ff7c570837dd8b911af64e9a48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/8818ac6cdc8d8424c483602d90b06efb00af5df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8e4d742df61e1e41db14fa4f92751dbf2b6057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d51624c34035f3cf1a7691d2dea514c26eca492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. However, each player plays each other once, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games in total.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/8379147b9512b14d813e15388ba9b5abf382a610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 + g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> therefore must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which only occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/76953c3888af8ff7c570837dd8b911af64e9a48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/8818ac6cdc8d8424c483602d90b06efb00af5df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> of the two options above.\n</p><p>Thus, the number of games that are tied is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/433d742232f7bf3512c11eb996630ff5ead3641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031928\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 119/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1050/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6086/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.984      1 2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    8.984      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35037:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018031928 and revision id 272001. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}